Mitcad patch (mitcad#343): the points of an OnSame end's cap on the face
at the end brought into one period however many periods apart.

A thread's flank rounded round its chamfer cone up to the root cylinder:
the rounding starts where the flank comes out of the root, an OnSame end
whose face at the end is the root cylinder. The bodies stored in files hold
such a cylinder trimmed to one period starting two turns below the basis
surface's parameters (u from -11.82 to -5.54), the face's edges' curves in
that range. The cap's point on the arc came from the arc's curve on the face
(u = -11.824) and the opposite contact's point from its projection on the
surface (u = 0.743, in the basis's range): two periods apart.
ChFi3d_Recale moved one of them by one period only, so the face's box for
the intersection spanned a whole period beside the cap and the blend's
intersection with the cylinder was not found ("OneCorner : echec calcul
intersection"). ChFi3d_Recale now brings the point not taken for reference
within half a period of the other by as many periods as they lie apart; for
points less than one and a half periods apart nothing changes.

